    "text": "KLTV\nwebsite\nWood County, Texas\nTeachers, former students highlight issues with poverty among students\n3 hours ago\n‘Be aware’: A&M AgriLife expert discusses snake threat around chicken coops. Those who raise chickens know it’s like ringing a dinner bell for any wildlife looking for an easy meal. Wood County chicken raiser Larry Hendrix has had to deal with it. “You would think I put up a Chick-Fil-A sign at the coop and the drive-thru was full.\" Most common raiders are raccoons going after the chickens, and snakes looking for eggs.",
